ress resilience/decision quality, and D also lacking data. We have already strong case for C, but also concerns about communication and egocentric, not willing to further education. B also has concerns. A has many unknowns, plus concerns: unorganized, unfriendly. D has concerns: weak leadership, moody, hot temper, loner, arrogant. So likely still C is best.\n\nThus we should reaffirm vote for Candidate C, perhaps argue that given lack of data for A and D, and the strengths of C outweigh concerns, we maintain recommendation for C.\n\nWe need to reference prior discussion: mention that Agent 3 highlighted missing data for A and D, and that we still see C as strongest.\n\nProvide explicit facts: C creates positive atmosphere, puts concern for others, makes correct decisions quickly, understands complicated technology, excellent attention skills. Concerns: difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. Argue that strengths in crew cooperation, decision quality, technical competence outweigh concerns, and that missing data for A and D makes them less viable.\n\nThus produce public message and metadata vote C."}
